  axis_only with 0 crossings and |d|@0.6 comparable to base's 0.417 would
  be the first variant that removes the wrap WITHOUT shrinking the step -
  which is exactly what the rescale failed to do, and why v37g found the
  rescale identical to base at matched |move|. TH0 then replaces the
  accidental k-coupling with an explicit, tunable step size.
